{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols"]]},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P9PlanarityE16_planarEdgeLimitSivp","roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"extension","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Planarity"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph’s planarity is that of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph.undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPlanar"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"planarEmbedding()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOuterplanar"},{"text":" run the left-right planarity test (de","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Fraysseix and Rosenstiehl, in Brandes’s formulation, 2009); ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()"},{"text":" runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Boyer and Myrvold’s edge-addition algorithm (2004), whose failure state isolates the witness.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"All are O(n + m), iterative, and deterministic: graphs with the same rows (the same vertices in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same order, the same edge positions, the same incidence order) get the same embedding and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same witness.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isOuterplanar","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPlanar"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/findKuratowskiSubgraph()","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarEmbedding()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"planarEmbedding()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A planar embedding of the graph, over every edge position (loops and parallel copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included), or nil when the graph is not planar: the witness of planarity. O(n + m), faces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarembedding()"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isOuterplanar":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isOuterplanar"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isouterplanar","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the graph has a planar embedding with every vertex on one face: whether the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus a new vertex joined to every vertex is planar. A simple graph with more than 2n − 3"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges is not. O(n + m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isOuterplanar","title":"isOuterplanar","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/findKuratowskiSubgraph()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"findKuratowskiSubgraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity18KuratowskiSubgraphV","text":"KuratowskiSubgraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"type":"topic","title":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subdivision of K₅ or K₃,₃ made of the graph’s edges, or nil when the graph is planar: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"witness of non-planarity. A dense graph is searched on its first 3n − 5 distinct pairs only,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which already hold one. O(n + m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/findKuratowskiSubgraph()","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/findkuratowskisubgraph()"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","role":"collection","title":"Planarity","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isPlanar":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isPlanar"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isplanar","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPlanar","abstract":[{"text":"Whether the graph can be drawn in the plane without crossing edges. A simple graph with more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than 3n − 6 edges is not, which is answered after counting distinct pairs, before any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"search. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"title":"isPlanar","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"to